[StudyName "En Passant Day 1 MCQ Classwork"]
[ChapterName "2. A Pawn May Move Two Squares Only From Its Starting Rank"]
[FEN "8/4k3/8/8/2p5/8/1P6/2K5 w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ [#] MCQ: Which move advances the white b-pawn two squares from its starting position?

A) b3
B) b4
C) Kb1
D) c3 }

1. b4 { Correct Answer: B) b4. A pawn may move two squares only on its first move from its starting rank, provided both squares are empty. } *


[Event "En Passant Day 1 MCQ Classwork"]
[Date "2026.07.31"]
[White "Student"]
[Black "MCQ"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[StudyName "En Passant Day 1 MCQ Classwork"]
[ChapterName "3. En Passant Is Triggered by a Two-Square Pawn Move"]
[FEN "8/4k3/8/8/1Pp5/8/8/2K5 b - b3 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ [#] MCQ: White has just played b2-b4. Which move is Black allowed to play?

A) c3
B) cxb3 en passant
C) Kf6
D) cxb4 }

1... cxb3 { Correct Answer: B) cxb3 en passant. Black captures the pawn as though it had moved only from b2 to b3. } *


