[StudyName "En Passant Day 1 MCQ Classwork"]
[ChapterName "4. The Two Pawns Must Be Side by Side"]
[FEN "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppp1p/8/1Pp3pP/8/8/P1PPPPP1/RNBQKBNR w KQkq g6 0 2"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ [#] MCQ: Why is White allowed to capture the black g-pawn en passant?

A) Pawns are allowed to capture straight forward.
B) The black pawn moved two squares and stopped beside the white h-pawn.
C) The white h-pawn is still on its starting square.
D) The black king is in check. }

2. hxg6 { Correct Answer: B. The pawns are side by side after Black's two-square pawn move, so White may capture en passant immediately. } *


