[StudyName "En Passant Day 1 MCQ Classwork"]
[ChapterName "6. The En Passant Right Is Lost After Any Other Move"]
[FEN "8/2k5/8/1pPK4/8/8/8/8 b - - 1 3"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ [#] MCQ: White played Kd5 instead of capturing the b-pawn en passant. Can White capture that pawn en passant on the next turn?

A) Yes, after the black king moves.
B) Yes, en passant remains available for the rest of the game.
C) No, the right expired when White played another move.
D) Only if the move gives check. }

3... Kd8 { Correct Answer: C. En passant is available only on the move immediately following the opponent's two-square pawn move. } *


